## DFF and 4-bit Counter

### Topic

Sequential logic, D flip-flop, counter, enable, and synchronous reset.

### What I Built

* `dff.v`
* `counter_4bit.v`
* `counter_4bit_tb.v`
* Counter simulation output
* Counter waveform screenshot
* README

### Main Files

```text
05_counter/
├── README.md
├── sim/
├── src/
├── tb/
└── waves/
```

### Waveform Files

```text
05_counter/waves/counter_4bit.vcd
05_counter/waves/counter_4bit_wave.png
05_counter/waves/counter_4bit_sim.png
```

### Key Takeaway

Sequential logic does not update immediately when an input changes.

The counter updates only on the rising edge of the clock:

```verilog
always @(posedge clk) begin
    ...
end
```

Important concepts:

* `clk = 1` is not the same as `posedge clk`
* `posedge clk` means the instant when `clk` changes from `0` to `1`
* `en` prepares the counter to increment
* `reset` clears the counter at the next clock edge because it is synchronous reset
* `#1` in the testbench allows the DUT output to update before checking

This day introduced the idea that registers store state and update only at clock edges.

